,p_name=>'WWV_FLOW_CUSTOM_AUTH_STD.ACTION4'
,p_message_text=>'The boolean result of the above block will be returned to the engine. If the result is true, the engine will continue to show or accept the page. If the result is false, the engine will redirect to the invalid session target specified in this authent'
||'ication scheme (see below).'
,p_version_scn=>37165770887607
);
wwv_flow_imp_shared.create_message(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(41397407375373543)
,p_name=>'WWV_FLOW_CUSTOM_AUTH_STD.ACTION5'
,p_message_text=>'The built-in method for session verification is available to the %0 developer using the API call:'
,p_version_scn=>37165770887607
);
wwv_flow_imp_shared.create_message(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(41397630513373578)
,p_name=>'WWV_FLOW_CUSTOM_AUTH_STD.ACTION6'
,p_message_text=>'This boolean function result can be combined with other checks in the user-provided page sentry function specified in an authentication scheme. If this API is called, it will check the cookie named %0'
,p_version_scn=>37165770887607
);
wwv_flow_imp_shared.create_message(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(41397800456373610)
,p_name=>'WWV_FLOW_CUSTOM_AUTH_STD.ACTION7'
,p_message_text=>'If the cookie exists and its decoded value locates a row in the internal sessions table, then the session is considered valid and a TRUE value is returned to the page sentry function that called it.'
,p_version_scn=>37165770887607
);
wwv_flow_imp_shared.create_message(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(41398205449373675)
,p_name=>'WWV_FLOW_CUSTOM_AUTH_STD.ACTION8'
,p_message_text=>'If the page sentry function returns TRUE, page rendering or processing continues. If the result is FALSE, the engine will show page %0, which is considered to be this application''s login page based on its designation in this authentication scheme as '
||'the invalid session page.'
,p_version_scn=>37165770887607
);
wwv_flow_imp_shared.create_message(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(41399028933373802)
,p_name=>'WWV_FLOW_CUSTOM_AUTH_STD.ACTION9'
,p_message_text=>'The page sentry function returns a boolean result to the engine. If the result is TRUE, page rendering or processing continues. If the result is FALSE, the engine will redirect to %0.'
,p_version_scn=>37165770887607
);
wwv_flow_imp_shared.create_message(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(41404428348374675)
,p_name=>'WWV_FLOW_CUSTOM_AUTH_STD.API_COMMON1'
,p_message_text=>'A typical approach is for the page to contain a login form to capture the user''s credentials. Then the page''s after-submit processes would call an authentication module to verify the credentials. After authentication, the page would perform any sessi'
||'on registration and cookie setting tasks. Finally it would redirect to the start page of the application.'
,p_version_scn=>37165770887607
);
wwv_flow_imp_shared.create_message(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(41404624149374709)
,p_name=>'WWV_FLOW_CUSTOM_AUTH_STD.API_COMMON2'
,p_message_text=>'The %0 API: wwv_flow_custom_auth_std can be called by such after-submit processes to perform any of these steps just described. There are two entry points available:'
,p_version_scn=>37165770887607
);
wwv_flow_imp_shared.create_message(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(41404827020374742)
,p_name=>'WWV_FLOW_CUSTOM_AUTH_STD.API_COMMON3'
,p_message_text=>'Call the login procedure to have the engine perform all of the steps for you. The engine will use the built-in sessions table and perform session registration and cookie setting for you. Any custom code you provide in this authentication scheme will '
||'be run at the pre-authentication, authentication, or post-authentication points.'
,p_version_scn=>37165770887607
);
wwv_flow_imp_shared.create_message(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(41405026585374778)
,p_name=>'WWV_FLOW_CUSTOM_AUTH_STD.API_COMMON4'
,p_message_text=>'Call the post_login procedure if you are performing authentication yourself but you would like %0 to handle all post-authentication chores for you. With these two entry points you can use any of the built-in login processing steps in combination with'
||' your own login page and any processes that run on it. Remember, if you use the built-in post-authentication processing, you can take advantage of built-in page sentry and session verification processing as well.'
,p_version_scn=>37165770887607
);
wwv_flow_imp_shared.create_message(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(41398420318373707)
,p_name=>'WWV_FLOW_CUSTOM_AUTH_STD.BUILTIN_LOGIN_PG'
,p_message_text=>'the built-in login page'
,p_version_scn=>37165770887607
);
wwv_flow_imp_shared.create_message(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(41405208647374810)
,p_name=>'WWV_FLOW_CUSTOM_AUTH_STD.CHART_LOGIN1'
,p_message_text=>'External Login Processing'
,p_version_scn=>37165770887607
);
wwv_flow_imp_shared.create_message(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(41407430774375234)
,p_name=>'WWV_FLOW_CUSTOM_AUTH_STD.CHART_LOGIN12'
,p_message_text=>'The login URL %0 does not appear to specify an %1 application page as the invalid session target. Additionally, there are no login processing values in the authentication scheme. This page is responsible for performing the following steps:'
,p_version_scn=>37165770887607
);
wwv_flow_imp_shared.create_message(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(41407619026375267)
,p_name=>'WWV_FLOW_CUSTOM_AUTH_STD.CHART_LOGIN13'
,p_message_text=>'Please note that unless the services invoked at this URL use the %0 wwv_custom_auth_std API to assist with session registration tasks, your application will not be able to use built-in page sentry or session verification processing. You will have to '
||'do this work by whatever means you devise on your own.'
,p_version_scn=>37165770887607
);
wwv_flow_imp_shared.create_message(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(41408407183375394)
,p_name=>'WWV_FLOW_CUSTOM_AUTH_STD.CHART_LOGIN14'
,p_message_text=>'The login URL %0 does not appear to specify an %1 application page as the invalid session target. This page is responsible for performing the following steps:'
,p_version_scn=>37165770887607
);
wwv_flow_imp_shared.create_message(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(41408604564375426)
,p_name=>'WWV_FLOW_CUSTOM_AUTH_STD.CHART_LOGIN15'
,p_message_text=>'The values set for login processing in the authentication scheme are shown below:'
,p_version_scn=>37165770887607
);
wwv_flow_imp_shared.create_message(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(41408805285375459)
,p_name=>'WWV_FLOW_CUSTOM_AUTH_STD.CHART_LOGIN16'
,p_message_text=>'The login page specified in this scheme is page [%0] in this application. This page is responsible for performing the following steps:'
,p_version_scn=>37165770887607
);
wwv_flow_imp_shared.create_message(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(41409023567375491)
,p_name=>'WWV_FLOW_CUSTOM_AUTH_STD.CHART_LOGIN17'
,p_message_text=>'However, there are no login processing values in the authentication scheme.'
,p_version_scn=>37165770887607
);
wwv_flow_imp_shared.create_message(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(41409231736375531)
,p_name=>'WWV_FLOW_CUSTOM_AUTH_STD.CHART_LOGIN18'
,p_message_text=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'Because this page is the designated login page for the application, it is not possible to perform certain actions on the page when the page is first shown, because user authentication has not yet occurred. Also, certain session state and session iden'
||'tification variables are not available to page computations or processes as they would be on ordinary pages that are processed after authentication. For these reasons, the specification of a login page by page number in an authentication scheme is on'
||'ly suitable for pages that have very little or no functionality other than login form processing. If you would prefer to have your login page be more active, please use the login URL designation in the authentication scheme wizard or edit page. So lo'
||'ng as you remember to set the public page attribute to ''Yes - This page is public'' using the page attributes form in the Builder the log',
'in page can use the full range of %0 features in addition to serving as the login page in your application.'))
,p_version_scn=>37165770887607
);
wwv_flow_imp_shared.create_message(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(41405431005374845)
,p_name=>'WWV_FLOW_CUSTOM_AUTH_STD.CHART_LOGIN2'
,p_message_text=>'This authentication scheme specifies neither a login page or a URL to be used for the invalid session target. This implies that the page sentry function handles this case. Perhaps it redirects to a single-signon portal or some other login server. Add'
||'itionally, there are no login processing values in the authentication scheme. If this is not what you intended, please edit this authentication scheme and provide an invalid session page or URL, then examine this chart view again.'
,p_version_scn=>37165770887607
);
wwv_flow_imp_shared.create_message(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(41405621034374879)
,p_name=>'WWV_FLOW_CUSTOM_AUTH_STD.CHART_LOGIN3'
,p_message_text=>'This authentication scheme specifies neither a login page or a URL to be used for the invalid session target. This implies that the page sentry function handles this case. Perhaps it redirects to a single-signon portal or some other login server. How'
||'ever, there are values set for login processing in the authentication scheme, as shown below:'
,p_version_scn=>37165770887607
);
wwv_flow_imp_shared.create_message(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(41405817398374910)
,p_name=>'WWV_FLOW_CUSTOM_AUTH_STD.CHART_LOGIN4'
,p_message_text=>'The login URL:%0 appears to specify an %1 application page as the invalid session target. However, there are no login processing values in the authentication scheme. This page is responsible for performing the following steps:'
,p_version_scn=>37165770887607
);
wwv_flow_imp_shared.create_message(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(41406230828374980)
,p_name=>'WWV_FLOW_CUSTOM_AUTH_STD.CHART_LOGIN6'
,p_message_text=>'In order for the %0 engine to be able to show or accept the login page in your application, you must select the page attribute ''Yes - This page is public'' on the Page Attributes page of the App Builder. If you do not do this, the engine will attempt '
||'to execute the page sentry function before showing the page. If you have not yet logged in, a redirect to the same URL will be attempted. This will cause a most unsatisfying loop. If you code your own page sentry function, you may need to recognize w'
||'hen the current page is this login page and handle it differently from other pages. If you can identify it by page number, fine. A more generic technique is to use the boolean function wwv_flow_custom_auth.current_page_is_public to recognize this pub'
||'lic attribute of the login page or any other page in your application.'
,p_version_scn=>37165770887607
);
wwv_flow_imp_shared.create_message(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(41406411682375060)
,p_name=>'WWV_FLOW_CUSTOM_AUTH_STD.CHART_LOGIN7'
,p_message_text=>'The login URL %0 appears to specify an %1 application page as the invalid session target. This page is responsible for performing the following steps:'
,p_version_scn=>37165770887607
);
wwv_flow_imp_shared.create_message(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(41406632730375093)
,p_name=>'WWV_FLOW_CUSTOM_AUTH_STD.CHART_LOGIN8'
,p_message_text=>'The values set for login processing in the authentication scheme are shown below:'
,p_version_scn=>37165770887607
);
wwv_flow_imp_shared.create_message(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(41406821282375137)
,p_name=>'WWV_FLOW_CUSTOM_AUTH_STD.CHART_LOGIN9'
,p_message_text=>'The Oracle Application Server Single Sign-On Server will redirect back to this application after user authentication. The entry point is the wwv_flow_custom_auth_sso.process_success procedure in the %0 schema. %0 is registered as an Oracle Applicatio'
||'n Server Single Sign-On partner application and can manage all interfaces to the login server for you. If, however, you would prefer to register your own application in your own schema, you can. You can write your own page sentry or simply create an '
||'authentication scheme based on the Portal-SSO scheme (my application as partner app) from the authentication scheme gallery. The resulting scheme will call the built-in SSO page sentry wwv_flow_custom_auth_std.portal_sso_sentry_v1. This function requ'
||'ires that the current authentication scheme knows the name of your partner application, as registered with Oracle Application Server Single Sign-On. The create authentication scheme wizard asks you for the partner application name, or it can be added'
||' or changed by editing the scheme after it is created. The name must be entered exactly as registered, observing case. You will also need to write your own URLC receiver procedure and call the wwv_flow_custom_auth_sso.process_success API from it, pas'
||'sing in the name of your application as you registered it with Oracle Application Server Single Sign-On. This will perform session registration with %0 after authentication. If you write your own page sentry, the wwv_flow_custom_auth_sso.portal_sso_r'
||'edirect API may be called by the page sentry to perform the redirect to the login server when it determines that authentication is required. You must pass in the registered name of your partner application to this procedure. Please consult the %0 doc'
||'umentation and the %1 documentation for details.'
,p_version_scn=>37165770887607
);
