,p_attribute_sequence=>4
,p_display_sequence=>40
,p_prompt=>'PL/SQL Code to Insert/Update/Delete'
,p_attribute_type=>'PLSQL'
,p_is_required=>true
,p_is_translatable=>false
,p_depending_on_attribute_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(3130191485054761)
,p_depending_on_has_to_exist=>true
,p_depending_on_condition_type=>'EQUALS'
,p_depending_on_expression=>'PLSQL_CODE'
,p_reference_scope=>'ROW'
,p_examples=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<pre>',
'begin',
'    case :APEX$ROW_STATUS',
'    when ''C'' then',
'        insert into emp ( empno, ename, deptno )',
'        values ( :P1_EMPNO, :P1_ENAME, :P1_DEPTNO )',
'        returning rowid into :P1_ROWID;',
'    when ''U'' then',
'        update emp',
'           set ename  = :P1_ENAME,',
'               deptno = :P1_DEPTNO',
'         where rowid  = :P1_ROWID;',
'    when ''D'' then',
'        delete emp',
'         where rowid = :P1_ROWID;',
'    end case;',
'end;',
'</pre>'))
,p_help_text=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<p>Enter PL/SQL code to process each row of data manipulated in the Form Region.</p>',
'<p>Use the page item name as a bind variable to access its value. The system variable <code>APEX$ROW_STATUS</code> returns the status of a row and can be used to check if the row has been created, updated or deleted (see example below for how to chec'
||'k this).</p>',
'<p><em>Note:</em> If primary key columns get populated by a trigger or in the PL/SQL code, it is a requirement that the new values are assigned to the bind variables of the primary key columns, because &PRODUCT_NAME. uses those values to fetch the ro'
||'w after an insert or update.</p>',
'<p>Oracle recommends calling procedures or functions within a PL/SQL package, to facilitate reuse and maintainability.</p>'))
);
wwv_flow_imp_shared.create_plugin_attribute(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(3133532996097347)
,p_plugin_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(3129968725049081)
,p_attribute_scope=>'COMPONENT'
,p_attribute_sequence=>5
,p_display_sequence=>50
,p_prompt=>'Prevent Lost Updates'
,p_attribute_type=>'CHECKBOX'
,p_is_required=>false
,p_is_common=>false
,p_show_in_wizard=>false
,p_default_value=>'Y'
,p_is_translatable=>false
,p_help_text=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<p>Specify whether processing should ensure that updates are not lost when multiple users update the same database record.</p> ',
'<p>Lost updates occur when two or more people try to update the same data, and the last update overwrites updates made by the first user to save changes. To prevent this from happening, updates can check the existing column value(s) in the database w'
||'ith the value(s) retrieved when the row was originally queried.</p>',
'<p>For example:',
'  <ol>',
'    <li>User A queries employee (EMP) records.</li>',
'    <li>User B queries the same employee records.</li>',
'    <li>User B updates employee details for EMPNO = 7839 and applies (commits) the changes to the database.</li>',
'    <li>User A Updates employee details for EMPNO = 7839 and is attempting to apply the changes to the database.</li>',
'  </ol>',
'If User A successfully updates the same row, changes made by User B will be lost.',
'When User A is attempting to save the employee row, then the data in the database is different from what User A queried originally. In step 1 above, the column value(s) originally queried by User A can be captured. Then in Step 4 above, the value(s) '
||'can be compared to the current values in the database. This comparison will raise an error for User A, as the database value(s) were updated by User B in Step 3. This prevents a user from overwriting changes made by another ',
'user to the same row.</p>',
'<p>Note</p>',
'<ul>',
'<li>How the lost updates are detected is specified in the Attributes for the Form region, based on the setting for <strong>Lost Update Type</strong>.</li>',
'<li>Lost Update Detection is <em>not available</em> for Form Regions using a <strong>REST Data Source</strong> and a <strong>Target Type</strong> of <strong>Table/View</strong> or <strong>PL/SQL Code</strong>.</li>',
'</ul>'))
);
wwv_flow_imp_shared.create_plugin_attribute(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(3134090605099409)
,p_plugin_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(3129968725049081)
,p_attribute_scope=>'COMPONENT'
,p_attribute_sequence=>6
,p_display_sequence=>60
,p_prompt=>'Lock Row'
,p_attribute_type=>'SELECT LIST'
,p_is_required=>true
,p_is_common=>false
,p_show_in_wizard=>false
,p_default_value=>'Y'
,p_is_translatable=>false
,p_lov_type=>'STATIC'
,p_help_text=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<p>Select whether each row to be updated or deleted is locked in the underlying table before processing the row.</p>',
'<p>Note: Lock Rows is <em>not available</em> for Form Regions using a <strong>REST Data Source</strong> and a <strong>Target Type</strong> of <strong>Table/View</strong> or <strong>PL/SQL Code</strong>.</p>'))
);
wwv_flow_imp_shared.create_plugin_attr_value(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(3134396093101055)
,p_plugin_attribute_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(3134090605099409)
,p_display_sequence=>10
,p_display_value=>'Yes'
,p_return_value=>'Y'
,p_help_text=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<p>Rows to be updated or deleted will be locked using SELECT ... FOR UPDATE to prevent other transactions being performed on the row until the transaction is committed.</p>',
'<p>Note - If an error is raised, such as for updatable views that do not support locking, then you may be able to utilize PL/SQL code to lock the driving table.</p>'))
);
wwv_flow_imp_shared.create_plugin_attr_value(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(3135017839102248)
,p_plugin_attribute_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(3134090605099409)
,p_display_sequence=>20
,p_display_value=>'No'
,p_return_value=>'N'
,p_help_text=>'Rows will not be locked.'
);
wwv_flow_imp_shared.create_plugin_attr_value(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(3135486454103394)
