,p_attribute_type=>'COLUMN'
,p_is_required=>false
,p_is_common=>false
,p_max_length=>128
,p_column_data_types=>'VARCHAR2:NUMBER:DATE:TIMESTAMP:TIMESTAMP_TZ:TIMESTAMP_LTZ:INTERVAL_Y2M:INTERVAL_D2S'
,p_is_translatable=>false
,p_parent_attribute_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(361800327927635543)
,p_help_text=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<p>Select the column that identifies the version of the row, this column does not need to be present on the page. Leave this attribute blank to use the built-in checksum.</p>',
'<p>Opportunistic locking uses lost update detection to ensure data integrity in applications where data can be accessed concurrently. &PRODUCT_NAME. can use a built in checksum to perform lost update detection and determine the version of the row. Th'
||'e checksum is a hash function of all the column values for the specific table row. It is retrieved when the record is queried from the database, and then compared against the hash of the current record in the database as part of <em>Automatic Row Pro'
||'cessing</em>. If the two values are the same then the update proceeds, otherwise an error is raised by Automatic Row Processing.</p>',
'<p>This attribute enables you to specify a single column which holds the row version, as an alternative to using the built-in checksum processing. This column should be updated whenever a record in the database is updated. Oracle recommends implement'
||'ing a ''Before Update'' database trigger on the table to increment or otherwise update the row version column. NUMBER columns are presumed to contain a sequence number for the row. However, DATE and TIMESTAMP columns can also be used. The advantage of '
||'using a single column is that the &PRODUCT_NAME. engine does not need to perform the hash of the complete row, instead it can just compare a single column value.</p>'))
);
wwv_flow_imp_shared.create_plugin_attribute(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(361804814168854679)
,p_plugin_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(361799714569626543)
