,p_display_sequence=>90
,p_prompt=>'Body HTML'
,p_attribute_type=>'HTML'
,p_is_required=>false
,p_is_translatable=>true
,p_depending_on_attribute_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(1801033763884282)
,p_depending_on_has_to_exist=>false
,p_depending_on_condition_type=>'NULL'
,p_help_text=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<p>Enter text that yields a multi-part HTML message, including both plain text and HTML content. The settings and capabilities of the recipient&#39;s email client will determine what displays. Although most modern email clients can read an HTML forma'
||'tted email, remember that some users disable this functionality to address security issues. Use substitution syntax, such as <code>&amp;P6_PRODUCT_NAME.</code>, if you want to include dynamic content in the text.</p>',
'<p>When referencing images using the &lt;img /&gt; tag, remember that the images must be accessible to the recipient&#39;s email client in order for them to see the image. For example, suppose you reference an image on your network called hello.gif a'
||'s follows:</p>',
'<pre>',
'&lt;img src=&quot;http://example.com/hello.gif&quot; alt=&quot;Hello&quot; /&gt;',
'</pre>',
'<p>In this example, the image is not attached to the email, but is referenced by the email. For the recipient to see it, they must be able to access the image using a Web browser. If the image is inside a firewall and the recipient is outside of the '
||'firewall, the image will not display. For this reason, avoid using images. If you must include images, be sure to include the ALT attribute to provide a textual description in the event the image is not accessible.</p>',
'<p><em>Note: The SMTP/MIME specification dictates that no single line shall exceed 1000 characters. To comply with this restriction, you must add a carriage return or line feed characters to break your text into chunks of 1000 characters or less. Fai'
||'ling to do so will result in erroneous email messages, including partial messages or messages with extraneous exclamation points.</em></p>'))
);
