,p_is_translatable=>false
,p_help_text=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<p>Specify whether matching values are retrieved from the database as the user types on the combobox item. <strong>Fetch on Search</strong> retrieves matching records from the database each time the user types a character. Otherwise, all of the list '
||'values are loaded on page load.</p>',
'<p>Oracle recommends using Fetch on Search when you have a large select list, as loading a large number of records may impact the time to initially load the page.</p>',
'<p>If attribute Fetch on Search is set to <strong>false</strong>, consolidation logic will be applied to avoid duplicated values, this is affected by the attribute <strong>Case Sensitive</strong> too. If Fetch on Search is set to <strong>true</strong'
||'>, no consolidation logic will be applied and LOV source cannot have a display column configured.</p>',
'<p>Example of data consolidation when LOV has only one column and attribute <strong>Case Sensitive</strong> is set to false: If the user types "blue", and on the Combobox data-set the option "Blue" exists, the value will be set to "Blue" and not "blu'
||'e". If the value doesn''t exists on the data-set the value would be set to what the user typed.</p>',
'<p>Example of data consolidation when LOV has return and display column configured and attribute <strong>Case Sensitive</strong> is set to false: If the user types "blue", the value would be set to the return value of the option. Following the blue e'
||'xample: If the option on the LOV is <strong>Display: Blue, Return: 15</strong> and the user types "blue", the value would be 15 and the display value would be set to "Blue". If the value doesn''t exists on the data-set, then the <strong>Manual Entries'
||' Item</strong> value would be set to "blue".</p>'))
);
