'<p>The specified item holds manual entered entries that are not found on the LOV data-set. Use this configuration if you are planning to further process the Combobox value, and you need to know if a value exists on the data-set or not.</p>',
'<p>It is required when the list of values has display and return columns configured. This would preferably be a hidden item, with the attribute <strong>Value Protected</strong> equal to false, therefore the value can be processed on the server. If <s'
||'trong>Multiple Values</strong> equal true, the Manual Entries Item would have its value separated in the same format as the item itself, using the attribute separator. The item value is updated unidirectionally from the Combobox item to Manual Entrie'
||'s Item, and not the other way around.</p>',
'<p>The use of this property will affect the session state content, where the Combobox item value will only contain the values that are part of the LOV data-set, to access the Manual Entries, developer has to check the session state content for the Ma'
||'nual Entries Item. This also applies to the JavaScript method apex.items.PX_ITEM_NAME.getValue, where it will return only the the values that are part of the LOV data-set too.</p>'))
);
wwv_flow_imp_shared.create_plugin_std_attribute(
 p_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(847953304099955894)
,p_plugin_id=>wwv_flow_imp.id(1449147321873942472)
,p_name=>'LOV'
,p_sql_min_column_count=>1
,p_sql_max_column_count=>2
,p_depending_on_has_to_exist=>true
,p_examples=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<dl>',
'<dt>Display and store same value in page item</dt>',
'<dd><pre>',
'select ename',
'  from emp',
' order by 1',
'</pre></dd>',
'<dt>Display employees of a specific department by using a bind variable</dt>',
'<dd><pre>',
'select ename',
'  from emp',
' where deptno = :P3_DEPTNO',
' order by 1',
'</pre>',
'<p>Note: Set <em>Cascading LOV Parent Item(s)</em> attribute to <code>P3_DEPTNO</code> if <code>P3_DEPTNO</code> is a modifiable page item on the same page.</dd>',
'</dl>'))
);
end;
/
