,p_accessibility_help_text=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<p>In the color picker UI, you can compare the color of a selected item with that of another item or a static value. This feature displays the contrast ratio between the two colors, aiding users in choosing colors that ensure accessibility for all in'
||'dividuals.</p>',
'<p>Contrast ratio refers to the difference in luminance or color between two elements in a design, typically the foreground (e.g., text or icons) and the background. A higher contrast ratio enhances readability and visibility, particularly for users '
||'with visual impairments or color vision deficiencies. The World Wide Web Consortium (W3C) recommends a minimum contrast ratio of 4.5:1 for normal text and 3:1 for large text (18pt or 14pt bold). </p>',
'<strong>Best practices</strong>:',
'<ol>',
'<li><strong>Contrast Ratio:</strong> Choose colors with a sufficient contrast ratio to ensure readability and visibility for all users. A higher contrast ratio between text and background colors is especially important for users with low vision or co'
||'lor blindness.</li>',
'<li><strong>Contrast checker:</strong> Utilize contrast checking tools to evaluate the color contrast ratio between foreground and background colors. Aim for a ratio of at least 4.5:1 for text and interactive elements to ensure readability for indivi'
||'duals with varying levels of vision impairment.</li>',
'</ol>'))
);
