,p_depending_on_expression=>'Y'
,p_help_text=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<p>Enter the color used for the text of this graph.',
'The color is specified using hexadecimal (hex) notation, RGB color codes, or HTML color names.</p>',
'<p>Hex notation is defined as #xxyyzz (a # followed by 3 double digit hex numbers), where xx, yy, and zz represent the two character hex values for red, green and blue respectively.',
'RGB codes are defined as RGB(xxx,xxx,xxx), where xxx is a number between 0 and 255 each representing the single 8-bit byte value for red, green, and blue respectively.</p>',
'<p>Search the internet for ''HTML Color Codes'' to find the equivalent hex code or RGB code for the color you wish to utilize.</p>'))
,p_important_for_accessibility=>true
,p_accessibility_help_text=>wwv_flow_string.join(wwv_flow_t_varchar2(
'<p>When it comes to accessibility, text colors should adhere to certain guidelines to ensure readability and inclusivity for all users, including those with visual impairments. Here are some best practices for choosing text colors:</p>',
'<strong>Best Practises:</strong>',
'<ol>',
'<li><strong>High Contrast:</strong> Text should have sufficient contrast against the background to ensure readability. The Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) recommend a minimum contrast ratio of 4.5:1 for normal text and 3:1 for large text '
||'(defined as text that is at least 18pt or 14pt bold).</li>',
'<li><strong>Avoid Pure Black and Pure White:</strong> While black text on a white background may seem like the default choice, pure black (#000000) and pure white (#FFFFFF) can create harsh contrasts that may strain the eyes. Slightly off-black and o'
||'ff-white shades are often easier on the eyes.</li>',
'<li><strong>Use of Red and Green:</strong> Red and green are particularly problematic for individuals with certain types of color blindness. If these colors are used to convey information, ensure that there are alternative ways to differentiate them '
||'(e.g., using patterns or labels).</li>',
'<li><strong>Consistency:</strong> Maintain consistency in text colors throughout your website or application to provide a cohesive experience for users. Inconsistencies in color usage can be confusing and detract from accessibility.</li>',
'<li><strong>Testing:</strong> Use accessibility testing tools to evaluate the contrast ratio of text colors against their background. These tools can help identify areas where contrast needs to be adjusted to meet accessibility standards.</li>',
'</ol>'))
);
